# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001114> (right lobe of liver)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "Wikipedia:Right_lobe_of_liver") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001114> "The right lobe is much larger than the left; the proportion between them being as six to one. It occupies the right hypochondrium, and is separated from the left lobe on its upper surface by the falciform ligament; on its under and posterior surfaces by the left sagittal fossa; and in front by the umbilical notch. It is of a somewhat quadrilateral form, its under and posterior surfaces being marked by three fossæ: the porta and the fossæ for the gall-bladder and inferior vena cava, which separate its left part into two smaller lobes; the quadrate and caudate lobes. [WP,unvetted].")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#date_retrieved> "2012-08-14") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#external_class> "TAO:0005173") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ontology> "TAO") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#source> "ZFIN:curator") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBPROP_0000001> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001114> "Portion of the liver which develops on the fish's right side adjacent to the gall bladder.[TAO]")
