AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0002048> "Snakes and limbless lizards typically possess only the right lung as a major respiratory organ; the left lung is greatly reduced, or even absent. Amphisbaenians, however, have the opposite arrangement, with a major left lung, and a reduced or absent right lung [WP]")
