# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004035> (cortical subplate)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "MP:0008440") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "Wikipedia:Subplate") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://github.com/obophenotype/mouse-anatomy-ontology/issues/1") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004035> "The transient outer neural tube region that contains the first generated post-mitotic neurons that receive synaptic input from thalamic axons and in turn project axons to the developing cortical plate.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#source> "WP") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBPROP_0000011> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004035> "The transient fetal subplate zone, together with the marginal zone and the cortical plate, represents the developmental anlage of the mammalian cerebral cortex. It serves as a waiting compartment for growing cortical afferents; its cells are involved in the establishment of pioneering cortical efferent projections and transient fetal circuitry, and apparently have a number of other developmental roles. The subplate zone is a phylogenetically recent structure and it is most developed in the human brain. Subplate neurons are among the first generated neurons in the mammalian cerebral cortex [1]. These neurons disappear during postnatal development and are important in establishing the correct wiring [2][3] and functional maturation [4] of the cerebral cortex. Subplate neurons appear to be selectively sensitive to injury (such as hypoxia) which in humans are associated with motor and cognitive defects")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "BRAINSPAN:BRAINSPAN") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonymType> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMO_0003000>) <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasBroadSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004035> "SP")
