# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0005068> (neural rod)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "GO:0014024") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "ZFA:0000133") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0005068> "A solid rod of neurectoderm derived from the neural keel. The neural rod is roughly circular in cross section. Neural rod formation occurs during primary neurulation in teleosts[GO]. An intermediate stage in the development of the central nervous system present during the segmentation period; the neural rod is roughly cylindrical in shape, forms from the neural keel, and is not yet hollowed out into the neural tube[ZFIN].")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#date_retrieved> "2012-08-14") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#external_class> "TAO:0000133") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ontology> "TAO") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#source> "ZFIN:curator") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBPROP_0000001> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0005068> "An intermediate stage in the development of the central nervous system present during the segmentation period; the neural rod is roughly cylindrical in shape, forms from the neural keel, and is not yet hollowed out into the neural tube. Kimmel et al, 1995.[TAO]")
