AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#date_retrieved> "2012-09-17") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#external_class> "VHOG:0001052") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ontology> "VHOG") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#source> "DOI:10.1046/j.1469-7580.2001.19910133.x Graham A. The development and evolution of the pharyngeal arches. J Anat (2001)") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#source> "http://bgee.unil.ch/") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBPROP_0000003> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0005691> "In all vertebrates, the pharyngeal apparatus develops from a series of bulges found on the lateral surface of the head, the pharyngeal arches, which consist of a number of different embryonic cell types. Each arch has an external covering of ectoderm and inner covering of endoderm, and between these a mesenchymal filling of neural crest with a central core of mesoderm.[well established][VHOG]")
